--- /dev/null
+++ b/openspec/changes/spatial-community-comment-cards/proposal.md
@@ -0,0 +1,14 @@
+# Spatial community comment cards (website only)
+
+The existing product and website both send numbered surface anchors without their approved comment text or attachment URLs. Their marker selection opens a generic Flutter comment panel; it does not display the corresponding content inside the model viewer. The renderer's existing preview card only expands on proximity, and its click handler emits an event without updating local selection. Identical marker payloads also replace the DOM nodes, which can interrupt an in-progress pointer interaction; live frequency of that replacement has not been established.
+
+Change the isolated website candidate so validated current-model comments send their existing text and API-provided media URLs through SharedSurfaceMarker. Clicking a pin selects and shows that one comment inside the same shared viewer, anchored by its unchanged root-local position and the existing Three.js projection/occlusion code. Freeze first-touch rotation before pointer release. Preserve an identical marker payload's DOM nodes. Keep the full comment list, author replies and authenticated composer behind the explicit all-comments entry. A near/selected surface layout must not automatically open the full list.
+
+The upstream reference is Sculpt ModelAnnotationCanvas.tsx revision 2e0e11d76650748ffd577b45943cd063cf097cb4, source SHA-256 b2270dd793eb6f3249395acf2c03dfc4979d3fb918d6a4f0f8c375ca059b383a. Sculpt supplies numbered, selectable root-associated HTML pins, click-versus-drag intent and occlusion semantics. This remains an adaptation: the existing Three.js renderer/root-local coordinates, content cards, zoom expansion and Supabase/Flutter integration are product behavior, not claims about Sculpt's original interface. No reconstruction algorithm, vendor engine, dependency or model input changes.
+
+A fixed website release query identifies the changed viewer iframe entry and its two changed ES-module URLs. Updating Flutter's main script alone is not assumed to invalidate nested stable ES-module URLs. Bundle verification continues to check exact resource hashes.
+
+Acceptance: red/green renderer selection/projection tests and a real WorkDetailPage/fake-transport integration test; no generic panel from pin clicks; approved text/images reach the iframe; anonymous private rows remain filtered; authenticated write and exact model-SHA gates remain; targeted Dart tests run with concurrency one, under 1.5 GiB process RSS; targeted analysis; unchanged upstream vendor/license bytes; fresh bundle manifest. Browser click hit testing, overlap/occlusion, spatial placement and publication remain separate root-owned live gates. No phone update or backend changes are authorized by this candidate.
+
+
+Paged polling is an additional concrete input-lifecycle fix: stage hot/latest refresh results and publish one validated snapshot. Do not emit empty markers merely because a refresh started. Initial independent sections and explicit pagination retain their existing behavior. Failed permissions/identity/model binding clear old remote content; unavailable reads also clear remote content and disable writes while preserving the user's unsent local draft. Responses and queued visibility callbacks remain bound to their load token and identity generation. This prevents unchanged periodic refreshes from deleting an expanded/pressed pin.
